  "answer": "### Short Answer\nAn individual is required to file an annual income tax return if their taxable income exceeds the threshold set by the tax rates, which is currently P250,000 for the taxable year.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe requirement for filing is governed by Section 24 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which outlines the income tax rates applicable to individuals.\n\n### Interpretation\nAccording to Section 24 of the NIRC, individuals, including citizens and resident aliens, are subject to income tax on their taxable income derived from all sources within and outside the Philippines. The tax rates are structured progressively, with the first P250,000 of taxable income being exempt from tax. Individuals whose income exceeds this threshold must file their income tax return.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, individuals earning more than P250,000 in a taxable year must file their annual income tax return to report their income and pay the corresponding tax. This filing is essential for compliance with tax obligations and to avoid penalties for non-filing.",
